proof_key_steps:
Auxiliary facts are proved inline (A1–A4):
- blow-up scaling;
- invariance of approximate tangent spaces under null modifications;
- locality through the upper density theorem;
- L^m(S) ≤ c^{-m}H^m(F(S)) on sets where F has lower Lipschitz constant c.

(TF), step A7. On a bilipschitz piece, four ingredients make the blow-ups of F(B) at F(b) converge to H^m⌞range DF(b):
- the area formula;
- the substitution a = b + rz;
- Lebesgue points of 1_B·J_F;
- differentiability at b.
Locality then transfers the tangent plane to any Borel Y ⊇ F(B) of finite measure, for L^m-a.e. b.

subproblems.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ with m ≥ 1, let X ∈ 𝒟_m(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ m) have compact support spt X and an integer multiplicity representation R = (M, θ, ξ) (IMRep univ m, R.Represents X), and let L : ℝ^P → ℝ^P be linear (Euclid P →L[ℝ] Euclid P). Then there is an integer multiplicity current Y ∈ 𝒟_m(ℝ^P) with:
- spt Y ⊆ L(spt X);
- ∂Y = 0 whenever ∂X = 0 (BoundaryVanishes X → BoundaryVanishes Y);
- Y(ω) = R.action(L^#ω) = ∫_M θ(x)·ξ(x)(ω(Lx)∘Λ^m L) dH^m(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟^m(ℝ^P), where L^#ω = affinePullbackForm L 0 ω.

Let P, m ∈ ℕ, let V ⊆ ℝ^P be a linear subspace with orthogonal projection q (V.starProjection), and let T, X, S' ∈ 𝒟_m(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ m). Assume:
- R_T and R_X are integer multiplicity representations of T and X (IMRep univ m);
- μ_{R_T}(ℝ^P ∖ V) = 0;
- spt X is compact;
- S'(ω) = T(ω) + R_X.action(q^#ω) for every ω ∈ 𝒟^m(ℝ^P), where q^#ω(x) = ω(qx)∘Λ^m q (affinePullbackForm q 0 ω).
Then there is an integer multiplicity triple R in ℝ^P (IMRep univ m) such that:
- R.action(ω) = T(ω) + X(ω) for every ω ∈ 𝒟^m(ℝ^P), so R represents T + X;
- M_O(S') ≤ μ_R(q^{-1}(O)) for every set O ⊆ ℝ^P (S'.massOn O ≤ R.measure (q⁻¹' O)).
